# `Option[T].map(f)` with `f` a VOID-returning `Callable` PARAMETER: the
# effect runs, the program exits 0 printing `hello%`, and NOTHING writes past
# the end of the `map` result slot on either lane.
#
# GRADUATED from `known_gaps/` (was `todo/t0729`'s repro). It stays a fixture
# in its own right because of the INSTRUMENT it is wired to: the live test
# builds it `--backend=llvm --sanitize` and runs it under `detect_leaks=1`.
# No other cell in the tree asserts that combination over this shape, and a
# value-only lane is STRUCTURALLY BLIND to the class — the emitted USER IR is
# not ASan-instrumented (only the runtime C is), so a stack out-of-bounds
# write surfaces only when it trips the `memcpy` interceptor's OVERLAP check,
# which needs the overrun to land EXACTLY on the source buffer. This cell's
# does. A plain `--backend=llvm` build of the broken compiler exited 0 with
# the right answer, correct BY LUCK.
#
# ── WHAT THE OVERRUN WAS ──
# The result slot of a void `map` is allocated `Option[int64]` — 16 bytes, 8
# tag + 8 payload — on BOTH lanes. The broken compiler then called the void
# callee through a fn-pointer cast typed from the RECEIVER (`Str(*)(...)`) and
# copied the resulting 32-byte `GorgetString` into that 8-byte field: on LLVM
# a 24-byte stack write past the end (the copy length came from the SOURCE
# value), on C a truncating 8-byte write (the length came from the DESTINATION
# field). Reading the callee's REAL signature removes the copy entirely — a
# `void` callee is called through a `void` function pointer and there is no
# value to store. `tests/fixtures/combinator_void_callable_spelling_axis.gg`
# pins the same read across every spelling of the callee.
#
# ⚠ THE `Callable` PARAMETER SPELLING IS LOAD-BEARING FOR THIS CELL: it is the
# one closure shape whose GIR local type is erased, so the declared return has
# to be recovered from the callable sidecar rather than read off the local.
# `mk` exists so the payload is a heap-built `String` and not a static
# literal — a static payload would not exercise the aggregate copy at all.
#
# ⊕ WHAT THIS FIXTURE DOES NOT DECIDE. The result TYPE of a void `map` is an
# open design question: the slot is still minted `Option[int64]` rather than
# the receiver's `Option[String]`. Nothing is written into it now, so the
# program is well-defined either way — but this fixture pins the ABSENCE OF
# THE OVERRUN, not the slot's type, and a future ruling on that type must
# leave this cell green.

String mk(String a, String b):
    return a + b

void shout(String s):
    print(mk(s, "%"))

void void_map(Callable[void(String)] f):
    Option[String] o = Some(mk("hel", "lo"))
    o.map(f)

void main():
    void_map(shout)
